WEBVTT

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.850
<b>July 11th, 2001</b>

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:10.480
<b>USSR Territory, Milkovsky District, Kamchatka.</b>

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:14.030
Why? Why today of all days?

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.590
Where's our fire support?

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:21.580
At this rate we'll be wiped out!

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.320
It's not coming! It's just too chaotic.

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:25.840
Nobody's seen any Laser Class yet.

00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:27.760
Air support should be possible.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:29.830
What is command doing?

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:32.060
They're here!

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:40.110
Help me!

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.390
Is this the end?

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:53.520
All units, weapons free.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.840
Let's show these lower 
life forms their place.

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:56.500
Roger.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:05.260
Captain!

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:08.790
Have you ever heard the legend 
of the Thunder God Perun?

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:10.880
The Slavic one?

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:14.340
The Thunder God has appeared before us!

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:17.960
Have all remaining forces form up 
and we'll begin a counterattack.

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:18.810
Yes sir.

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:00.900
<b>August 4th, 2001</b>

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:06.240
We will be docking in 
Petropavlovsk-Kamchatsky in approximately 30 minutes.

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:09.490
Prepare to disembark.

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:14.010
So this is the Soviet's biggest 
military base in the far east?

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:18.330
It's in pretty good shape for 
something on the front lines.

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:21.590
What's that mountain? It's huge.

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:23.510
Avachinsky, I think it's called.

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:30.340
I can't believe they dragged us all the way 
out from the sunny Caribbean to Kamchatka.

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:32.060
We don't have a choice.

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:37.430
It's part of our job as test pilots to get 
data in all kinds of environmental conditions.

00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:41.910
That's not it. I'm not worried 
about something as minor as that.

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:42.540
Minor?

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:48.720
If it's so cold outside how am I going to 
get to see Princess Yui in her bathing suit?

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:51.290
An idiot. He's a genuine idiot.

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:53.230
I want to go back to the Caribbean!

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:55.290
Then go! Start swimming!

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:02.330
What's wrong, Yuuya?

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:03.730
Nothing.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:09.520
An enemy attack?

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:10.950
Not by the looks of it.

00:04:16.550 --> 00:04:18.430
That's a... Cheburashka?

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:19.770
No, an Aligatori?

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:21.900
One of them's in trouble!

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:24.770
He needs to bail-out!

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:27.290
He didn't?

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:31.020
Looks like he couldn't.

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:35.100
The frame must've gotten bent 
in melee combat or something.

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:36.300
It happens a lot.

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:38.670
Can you feel it, Yuuya?

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:43.170
This is how the air feels on the battlefield.

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:50.100
The Far East Front Lines

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:56.100
<b>UN Far North Naval Theatre 6th Army</b>

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:56.100
<b>Petropavlovsk-Kamchatsky Base</b>

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:04.860
Forward! Forward!

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:06.840
Careful with that thing!

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:08.940
Going well?

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:10.540
Hey there. How about you?

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:14.720
I don't have much to unpack.

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:16.260
Not that.

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:18.470
Princess Yui.

00:05:18.470 --> 00:05:21.880
You haven't really talked to her since that 
night you spent on the island, have you?

00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:25.140
What are you talking about, moron?

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:28.630
Cryska, no, Ensign Barchenowa was there, too.

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:34.400
From the sound of it, you got pretty close to 
one of the Scarlet Twins while you were at it.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.590
Enough already.

00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:39.730
The Soviet Areas were off-limits, I told you!

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:43.300
The so-called "Iron Curtain", huh?

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:45.060
Too bad.

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:48.600
Not really. I'm not here to make friends.

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:52.750
Well, don't get all stiff because 
it's your first real fighting test.

00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:53.980
I'm not!

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:54.730
Now now.

00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:56.890
That's what I'm talking 
about when I say "stiff".

00:05:56.890 --> 00:05:58.310
Shut up.

00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:00.020
Don't tell me to shut up.

00:06:02.530 --> 00:06:05.340
The goal of these international 
joint exercises

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:10.640
is to test how well the Type 94 and 
Active Eagle respond in real combat.

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:17.510
And we'll also be testing a new 
prototype weapon delivered from Japan.

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:21.030
Lt. Takamura will explain.

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:31.950
As part of our evaluations, we'll also be 
testing the Prototype Type 99 EM Radiation Cannon.

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:42.390
Furthermore, the Shiranui Type 
2 will be the one testing it.

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:49.670
Tests are being done with the Shiranui 
and Shiranui Type 1c in Japan,

00:06:49.670 --> 00:06:54.090
but of course, this will be the 
first test with the Shiranui Type 2.

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:59.600
Unexpected problems may 
occur during the test,

00:06:55.740 --> 00:07:00.010
Sure, it's a new railgun, but it's 
still a long-range support weapon.

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:01.370
and you'll need to be able 
to respond accordingly.

00:07:00.590 --> 00:07:03.970
It's my first test in the Type 94 Second,

00:07:03.970 --> 00:07:06.100
and they won't let me fight up close?

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:19.990
Ensign Bridges.

00:07:21.050 --> 00:07:21.940
W-What?

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:24.750
No... I'm sorry I scared you.

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:25.450
And?

00:07:26.190 --> 00:07:29.540
Do you want to go see the new 
weapon you'll be testing?

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:32.970
I thought it'd be better for 
you to see it for yourself.

00:07:33.510 --> 00:07:35.850
I'd like to explain some more things, too.

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:39.720
Yeah, I'd like to if I could, I guess.

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:42.480
I see... I'm glad.

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:47.050
What are they doing?

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.490
No, nothing.

00:07:58.690 --> 00:07:59.660
This is...

00:08:00.140 --> 00:08:02.200
A next-generation TSF weapon.

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:04.580
The Prototype Type 99 EM Radiation Cannon.

00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:09.580
I guarantee you it packs 
enough stopping power.

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:12.920
I've worked on its development, 
if only for a short while.

00:08:13.330 --> 00:08:16.700
I believe it... but this worries me a little.

00:08:17.210 --> 00:08:17.920
Worries you?

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:23.900
I'm sure it's powerful, but you're giving 
up a lot of maneuverability to use it.

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:28.610
I bet it would wreck your aerodynamics 
and center of gravity.

00:08:29.910 --> 00:08:35.740
It feels to me like it doesn't work with 
the design principles of the 94 Second.

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:38.200
What's wrong?

00:08:38.970 --> 00:08:39.690
Well...

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:43.070
I'll admit it doesn't work 
with the design concepts.

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:45.970
But we're backed into a corner here.

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:51.370
By the way, well...

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:53.970
I'm sorry.

00:08:54.910 --> 00:08:57.480
I had the wrong idea about you.

00:08:57.480 --> 00:08:58.430
The wrong idea?

00:08:59.460 --> 00:09:02.780
I thought you might be sulking because

00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:05.980
you had to deal with something like 
this during your first extra fight?

00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:13.470
But you easily pointed out the flaw 
with the design concept at a glance,

00:09:14.090 --> 00:09:16.210
so I can see I was mistaken.

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:18.060
No, I...

00:09:18.060 --> 00:09:22.370
Actually, there was a bit of a dispute 
before these exercises were scheduled.

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:28.410
As lead developer, I cannot allow 
combat trials at this point!

00:09:28.740 --> 00:09:30.210
I know.

00:09:30.740 --> 00:09:33.550
But the decision was made by UN Command.

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:38.060
The Japanese Government has agreed 
to the combat trials in the U.S.S.R.

00:09:38.830 --> 00:09:40.040
The Japanese Government?

00:09:44.130 --> 00:09:47.400
Lt. Takamura, think about this realistically.

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:52.560
It looks like there's some kind of 
international bargain going on here.

00:09:53.380 --> 00:09:56.140
There's almost no chance the 
trials will be called off.

00:09:56.400 --> 00:10:00.020
Which means there's only 
one thing for us to do.

00:10:02.180 --> 00:10:04.660
Make sure the people we 
send there come back alive.

00:10:05.020 --> 00:10:06.320
That's right.

00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:08.360
And not lose a single one of them.

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:11.700
We'll do everything we can for that.

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:13.500
Just focus on that.

00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:18.010
A dispute?

00:10:18.310 --> 00:10:20.190
No, don't worry about it.

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:22.680
More importantly, I have a request.

00:10:23.090 --> 00:10:23.630
A request?

00:10:24.050 --> 00:10:25.590
This is a war zone.

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:31.420
If you think it's slowing you down, 
feel free to discard the weapon.

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:35.910
But if you do, make sure you activate 
the self-destruct switch inside it.

00:10:36.410 --> 00:10:40.900
I see. So this is a military secret you 
don't want the other nations getting.

00:10:41.500 --> 00:10:42.920
For now.

00:10:43.340 --> 00:10:46.940
But some day it will probably 
be standard equipment worldwide.

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:52.030
Once the technology is proven, weapons and 
TSFs get budgets and get mass-produced.

00:10:52.030 --> 00:10:53.430
Well, that's true.

00:10:54.160 --> 00:10:56.970
But you can't do that with talented Eishi.

00:10:57.630 --> 00:11:04.030
So I don't want to lose either 
the Shiranui Type 2...

00:11:07.240 --> 00:11:10.850
Or you, its lead test pilot.

00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:14.260
Don't forget that.

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:16.630
Y-Yeah.

00:11:20.090 --> 00:11:21.120
Eight minutes.

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:25.810
That's how long the average soldier 
lasts in their first battle.

00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:27.720
The eight minutes of death?

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:28.970
I've heard of it.

00:11:28.970 --> 00:11:30.920
We learn it in the US Military too.

00:11:31.400 --> 00:11:34.440
But that includes the first 
battles in Europe and Asia,

00:11:34.440 --> 00:11:37.170
which were fought in first-generation TSFs.

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:37.700
Lately...

00:11:37.700 --> 00:11:38.680
I...

00:11:40.060 --> 00:11:44.110
I lost a lot of friends 
in those eight minutes.

00:11:54.260 --> 00:11:56.260
So I don't...

00:11:56.260 --> 00:11:57.470
I know.

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:02.830
No matter how much practice 
I've had in the US military,

00:12:02.830 --> 00:12:05.480
it's true that I've never 
had any combat experience.

00:12:06.350 --> 00:12:10.870
So I won't underestimate real 
combat. I won't doubt the data.

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:14.010
And so I promise you.

00:12:14.010 --> 00:12:17.000
I'll bring your beloved 94 
Second back without a scratch.

00:12:18.180 --> 00:12:18.970
I promise.

00:12:21.110 --> 00:12:23.140
This EM cannon too.

00:12:23.710 --> 00:12:27.360
Honestly, I was little upset.

00:12:27.360 --> 00:12:31.590
This thing's gonna wreck my combat test.

00:12:31.590 --> 00:12:35.400
But after talking with you I 
don't care about that anymore.

00:12:38.210 --> 00:12:39.330
I see.

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:43.810
Lt. Takamura, Lt. Ibrahim is waiting 
for you in Conference Room 3.

00:12:46.020 --> 00:12:47.240
Oh no.

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:50.250
I was supposed to have a meeting 
with the base officers.

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:51.730
You should get going.

00:12:51.730 --> 00:12:53.070
S-Sorry.

00:12:54.810 --> 00:12:55.320
Lieutenant!

00:12:55.930 --> 00:12:56.910
Thank you.

00:12:57.940 --> 00:12:59.750
I'm glad I got to see it up close.

00:13:00.520 --> 00:13:02.210
It helped.

00:13:02.810 --> 00:13:04.960
I see. I'm glad to hear that.

00:13:19.380 --> 00:13:22.720
I don't like this place.

00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:25.530
What? Something wrong?

00:13:25.890 --> 00:13:26.980
Just a bit ago...

00:13:31.630 --> 00:13:32.630
Excuse me.

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:35.500
I thought the PX was around here somewhere.

00:13:36.090 --> 00:13:38.100
Do you know what a PX is?

00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:43.440
What's so funny?

00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:44.580
Do zavtra.

00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:46.000
Hey!

00:13:47.070 --> 00:13:49.610
Well, to the locals we're just a nuisance.

00:13:49.610 --> 00:13:51.960
But that doesn't give them an 
excuse not to work with us.

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:56.100
Not sharing information.

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:57.850
Not keeping us in the loop.

00:13:57.850 --> 00:14:00.980
Not treating us properly.

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:02.200
None of those are good things.

00:14:02.870 --> 00:14:04.920
You're more harsh than usual.

00:14:06.010 --> 00:14:10.120
I suppose given the history between the 
U.S.S.R. and Sweden, it's understandable.

00:14:10.500 --> 00:14:12.520
I'm just telling the truth.

00:14:13.060 --> 00:14:18.430
But I'm guessing there's not enough 
manpower, not enough supplies, not enough everything.

00:14:18.430 --> 00:14:21.620
I can see how they wouldn't 
want to talk to somebody

00:14:21.620 --> 00:14:23.800
who came from the safety of the rear lines.

00:14:24.260 --> 00:14:29.450
And now Tarisa's acting sympathetic, huh?

00:14:29.450 --> 00:14:30.770
Don't make fun of me.

00:14:30.770 --> 00:14:34.310
I'm just saying I know how 
it feels on the front lines.

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:35.510
Yeah, true.

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:42.880
Anyway, we'll be fine, but I 
wonder if Yuuya will be okay.

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:45.340
I hope he doesn't end up on the 
wrong end of something bad.

00:14:46.730 --> 00:14:49.930
You're worried about him, aren't you?

00:14:49.930 --> 00:14:50.690
Do you have a crush?

00:14:58.770 --> 00:15:00.010
Crap.

00:15:00.760 --> 00:15:03.740
Our barracks is supposed to 
be around here somewhere.

00:15:05.010 --> 00:15:09.730
Come to think of it, it felt like 
this when I was following Inia too.

00:15:22.470 --> 00:15:24.010
This is her...

00:15:24.010 --> 00:15:26.650
You can't even apologize?

00:15:27.150 --> 00:15:28.950
You think you're on a sightseeing tour here?

00:15:31.300 --> 00:15:34.170
Hey, she's got a cute face.

00:15:34.170 --> 00:15:37.070
Let me take a better look.

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:43.240
Or do you not want to talk 
to dirty people like us?

00:15:43.700 --> 00:15:45.110
Cryska...

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:47.770
It's fine. It's fine, Inia.

00:15:48.310 --> 00:15:50.050
Are you listening to us?

00:15:50.050 --> 00:15:51.650
I...

00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:57.620
I am a test pilot with the 331st 
Special Experimental Development Squad

00:15:57.620 --> 00:16:01.580
of the Soviet Central 
Strategic Research Corps.

00:16:01.580 --> 00:16:03.070
Ensign Cryska Barchenowa.

00:16:03.520 --> 00:16:07.700
Right, right. An elite from the capital.

00:16:07.700 --> 00:16:09.680
So what of it?

00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:14.670
We're supposed to be comrades, 
fighting for the motherland. Why?

00:16:14.670 --> 00:16:15.570
Comrades?

00:16:21.430 --> 00:16:22.570
Shut the hell up.

00:16:23.190 --> 00:16:24.640
The motherland?

00:16:25.160 --> 00:16:27.280
Don't make me laugh.

00:16:27.280 --> 00:16:28.830
What do you mean?

00:16:29.210 --> 00:16:30.740
We're both soldiers in the Soviet-

00:16:30.740 --> 00:16:31.750
No.

00:16:31.750 --> 00:16:33.120
You're a Russian.

00:16:35.060 --> 00:16:36.870
What the hell is a "Soviet" anyway?

00:16:36.870 --> 00:16:39.260
It's not even the name of a country.

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:44.680
We know that it was almost all 
Russians who escaped to Alaska.

00:16:45.190 --> 00:16:50.270
Georgians and Kazakhs like 
us are treated like garbage!

00:16:50.680 --> 00:16:56.810
We're the ones dying out here, while you 
guys are slacking off on the rear lines!

00:17:01.160 --> 00:17:02.150
Cryska?

00:17:03.200 --> 00:17:04.470
Cryska!

00:17:04.470 --> 00:17:04.990
Cryska?

00:17:04.990 --> 00:17:06.290
What's her problem?

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:08.330
Did she get scared and piss her pants?

00:17:09.740 --> 00:17:15.610
Your TSF is that purple 
Terminator in hangar 48 right?

00:17:16.310 --> 00:17:18.030
It's...

00:17:18.030 --> 00:17:21.800
You get that fancy machine 
and you're not even fighting?

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:24.150
Cryska! Cryska!

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:26.380
Stop it! Stop it!

00:17:26.850 --> 00:17:29.490
This little kid is a brat.

00:17:29.490 --> 00:17:32.410
Want to strip her and tie 
her to the fence like usual?

00:17:32.950 --> 00:17:35.970
Then let's head to hangar 8 like usual.

00:17:35.970 --> 00:17:38.370
The guys there are always hungry.

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:39.510
Wait.

00:17:39.510 --> 00:17:43.800
If we're gonna let them have these 
two, we should enjoy them first.

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:46.050
You enjoy it too, don't you?

00:17:46.970 --> 00:17:49.020
Okay, I'll take the little one.

00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:50.310
No!

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:52.570
Come on, get over here.

00:17:52.570 --> 00:17:54.720
Cryska!

00:17:53.620 --> 00:17:55.140
Stop it, please...

00:17:55.140 --> 00:17:58.450
That girl, Inia, is...

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:02.720
This little kid's probably 
useless on the battlefield.

00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:04.070
No!

00:18:04.070 --> 00:18:05.170
Inia is...

00:18:06.360 --> 00:18:07.330
What's wrong?

00:18:07.720 --> 00:18:09.590
She's not useless.

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:13.960
Let's have some fun, girl.

00:18:14.410 --> 00:18:17.370
Stop it! Cryska! Cryska!

00:18:17.780 --> 00:18:20.350
"Cryska! Cryska!"

00:18:20.820 --> 00:18:22.570
Stop it!

00:18:25.910 --> 00:18:28.160
Yuuya Bridges...

00:18:33.960 --> 00:18:35.210
What's your problem?

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:36.660
You think you're a big hero or something?

00:18:38.040 --> 00:18:39.200
Are you okay?

00:18:39.200 --> 00:18:40.350
Cryska...

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:43.200
I'm fine.

00:18:44.180 --> 00:18:46.420
Please take care of Inia.

00:18:47.900 --> 00:18:51.720
Why is Cryska just letting this happen?

00:18:53.110 --> 00:18:54.670
Hey, brats.

00:18:54.670 --> 00:18:55.980
What mechanic squad are you assigned to?

00:18:56.390 --> 00:18:57.160
What?

00:18:57.500 --> 00:18:58.590
The hell?

00:18:58.970 --> 00:19:00.160
Can't you see this?

00:19:00.680 --> 00:19:01.660
A wing mark?

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:04.920
These are Eishi?

00:19:06.300 --> 00:19:08.620
They're all kids!

00:19:09.800 --> 00:19:12.970
I think I saw you in the port.

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:16.160
You one of the cowards from Alaska?

00:19:17.440 --> 00:19:18.790
Damn it.

00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:23.150
Sorry, mister.

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:27.400
This isn't like the safe bases at the rear.

00:19:28.230 --> 00:19:31.310
You can scream but the MPs won't come.

00:19:31.310 --> 00:19:34.740
You're going to pay for hurting my buddy.

00:19:37.970 --> 00:19:40.020
What are you doing?

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:43.480
Tasha?

00:19:43.480 --> 00:19:44.270
That means...

00:19:44.630 --> 00:19:48.590
I don't know why you think you have 
time to be playing with our guests.

00:19:50.900 --> 00:19:52.890
The welcome party is over.

00:19:52.890 --> 00:19:56.860
Return to your posts and check 
on your TSF's maintenance status.

00:19:57.450 --> 00:19:59.390
U-Understood Commander.

00:19:59.390 --> 00:20:00.040
Let's go.

00:20:03.870 --> 00:20:04.760
Um...

00:20:10.680 --> 00:20:12.390
Thank you, Commander.

00:20:12.540 --> 00:20:13.220
You save-

00:20:12.540 --> 00:20:14.940
Know your place here.

00:20:15.340 --> 00:20:15.910
Understood?

00:20:27.470 --> 00:20:28.610
What the hell?

00:20:36.140 --> 00:20:37.570
Okay, stop.

00:20:37.980 --> 00:20:40.300
We'll start placing the sonic sensors.

00:20:45.710 --> 00:20:46.890
What's wrong?

00:20:46.890 --> 00:20:48.890
I don't like this.

00:20:48.890 --> 00:20:51.770
Where'd those annoying birds go?

00:20:53.700 --> 00:20:55.660
Yeah, it's strangely quiet.

00:21:02.140 --> 00:21:06.570
This is an analysis of an image captured 
by a warning satellite early this morning.

00:21:22.220 --> 00:21:28.260
Pay close attention to Evensk Hive SSW 
Group F and Okhotsk Coast Group K.

00:21:28.890 --> 00:21:30.860
This data is 18 hours old.

00:21:31.480 --> 00:21:36.750
The Far East Soviet Forces believe that K 
Group will land on the Okhotsk shore in 6 hours.

00:21:37.170 --> 00:21:39.980
Between 24 and 72 hours from now,

00:21:39.980 --> 00:21:46.370
a large group of BETA that are currently on 
the bottom shore will start landing as well.

00:21:50.580 --> 00:21:51.870
Given this,

00:21:52.380 --> 00:21:58.320
we will be accompanying the Soviet forces 
whose mission it is to repel the landing,

00:21:58.320 --> 00:22:01.110
and performing our first combat trials there.

00:22:02.060 --> 00:22:03.800
It's finally time, huh?

00:22:03.800 --> 00:22:06.680
I was getting sick of the crappy food here.

00:22:06.680 --> 00:22:08.630
It'll be a good way to kill some time.

00:22:08.630 --> 00:22:12.270
Will it? I think there are too many 
of them to let our guard down.

00:22:13.210 --> 00:22:15.640
Furthermore, Argos Test flight will be paired

00:22:15.640 --> 00:22:19.190
with the aces of the Far East 
Soviet Army, the Zhar Battalion.

00:22:20.670 --> 00:22:22.600
I'll introduce the commander.

00:22:23.510 --> 00:22:25.100
Everyone, stand!

00:22:31.860 --> 00:22:32.880
That's...

00:22:33.340 --> 00:22:34.610
Salute!

00:22:36.580 --> 00:22:40.250
I am Commander Fikatsia Latrova, 
of the Zhar Batallion.

00:24:07.140 --> 00:24:09.360
Do whatever you want.

00:24:09.360 --> 00:24:11.010
But don't get in our way.

00:24:11.400 --> 00:24:14.070
Something's not right here.

00:24:14.070 --> 00:24:16.110
I hope it's just my imagination...

00:24:16.110 --> 00:24:19.160
Let's go, monsters!

00:24:17.050 --> 00:24:24.350
<b>Falling Tears</b>

00:24:19.740 --> 00:24:22.970
Next time on Total Eclipse: Falling Tears
